From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: keep ARP and ND offload off on Apple firmware while awake

brcmfmac enables the firmware's ARP and IPv6 ND offload (ndoe) whenever
the interface is up and not promiscuous. On the Apple firmware ndoe
makes IPv6 downloads collapse. MacBookPro15,1 (BCM4364/3, FWID
01-47278712), 20 s IPv6 downloads on a 120 Mbit/s line: 58 and
42 Mbit/s with ndoe on, 108 to 120 Mbit/s with this patch.

macOS runs these offloads only in sleep. AppleBCMWLANCoreMac enables
them in configurePktFilters, called from configureWoWEntry and
configureLPASEntry, and disables them on wake. Keep them off on boards
whose board type starts with "apple,".

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
@@ -104,6 +104,17 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/* macOS enables ARP and ND offload on the Apple firmware only on
+	 * entering sleep with an association and disables them on wake. With
+	 * ND offload on while awake, the firmware logs an error for nearly
+	 * every received frame and downloads drop to about 55 Mbit/s.
+	 */
+	if (enable && ifp->drvr->settings->board_type &&
+	    strstarts(ifp->drvr->settings->board_type, "apple,")) {
+		brcmf_dbg(TRACE, "Skip ARP/ND offload enable on Apple firmware\n");
+		enable = false;
+	}
+
 	if (enable)
 		mode = BRCMF_ARP_OL_AGENT | BRCMF_ARP_OL_PEER_AUTO_REPLY;
 	else
